    "narrative": "Our offensive core is anchored today by **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), who both benefit significantly from favorable matchups against shaky pitching. **Lawrence Butler** is our strongest play, taking advantage of an excellent projection against Tyler Phillips, where a combination of park factors and a strong platoon edge pushes him to an elite tier. Similarly, **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) are primed for high-contact production against Ryan Feltner; the high-run-environment park and Feltner\u2019s elevated xERA provide a clear ceiling for both. **Jonathan Aranda** (66.98) also earns a premium spot, with his underlying xwOBA metrics suggesting he is due for positive regression against Spencer Arrighetti, reinforcing his standing as a mandatory start in the 2-hole.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Geraldo Perdomo** (50.71). While he offered a respectable score, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Drew Gilbert** (62.66), who draws a favorable platoon advantage against Feltner. **Perdomo**\u2019s proximity to a start was dampened by the presence of a strong opposing arm in Kyle Harrison, whose elite skill set acted as a negative multiplier for our middle infield depth. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Cal Raleigh** (41.14); facing an elite arm like Dylan Cease severely suppresses his output, keeping him strictly in the marginal category. Note that with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** still sidelined on the IL and **Bryson Stott** off the schedule, we are leaning heavily on our outfield depth\u2014specifically **Dylan Beavers** (66.64) and **Taylor Ward** (57.98)\u2014to generate the necessary volume to maintain our standing in the SB and R categories. All projected positions remain fluid pending final lineup cards; monitor these closely to ensure no last-minute scratches compromise our daily efficiency.",
